// MP+na+rlx -- the data is non-atomic and the flag relaxed, so the data
// accesses race: undefined behaviour under RC11 and ORC11, whose race detector
// flags every race RC11 does. RAR has no non-atomic accesses and refuses this
// program.
//
// RC11 and the two models defined on fragments of it: ORC11 (Dang, Jourdan,
// Kaiser & Dreyer, POPL 2020), RC11 without SC accesses or SC fences, and RAR
// (Doherty, Dongol, Wehrheim & Derrick, PPoPP 2019), its release-acquire/relaxed
// fragment. On a program inside a fragment, each answers as RC11 does: ORC11 by
// the correspondence its paper sketches, RAR by the equivalence its paper
// proves. herd7 under rc11.cat agrees with RC11 on this file.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x.store(1, na);
  y.store(1, rlx)
} ||| {
  r1 := y.load(rlx);
  if (r1 = 1) {
    r2 := x.load(na)
  } else {skip}
}
%%
allow (ub) [RC11, ORC11]
